codebase-memory-mcp 0.11.0

Usage:
  codebase-memory-mcp              Run MCP server on stdio
  codebase-memory-mcp cli [--quiet] [--progress] [--verbose] [--json] <tool> [args]
                                      Run one tool locally, then exit
  codebase-memory-mcp install [-y|-n] [--force] [--dry-run] [--dir=<path>] [--skip-config]
                                      [--clients=<tokens>]  Run 'install --clients' to list tokens
  codebase-memory-mcp uninstall [-y|-n] [--dry-run]
  codebase-memory-mcp update [-y|-n]
  codebase-memory-mcp config <list|get|set|reset>
  codebase-memory-mcp --version    Print version
  codebase-memory-mcp --help       Print this help

CLI output options:
  --quiet       Show errors only; disable automatic terminal progress
  --progress    Show lifecycle progress even with redirected stderr
  --verbose     Include informational diagnostics
  --json        Print the raw MCP result envelope
  --quiet cannot be combined with --progress or outer --verbose.

UI options:
  --ui=true    Enable HTTP graph visualization (persisted)
  --ui=false   Disable HTTP graph visualization (persisted)
  --port=N     Set UI port (default 9749, persisted)
  --tool-profile=analysis|scout  Expose a restricted inspection surface

Supported automatic/conditional client surfaces (45):
  Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, Zed, OpenCode,
  Antigravity, Aider, KiloCode, VS Code, Cursor, Windsurf,
  Augment / Auggie, OpenClaw, Kiro, Junie, Hermes, OpenHands,
  Cline, Warp, Qwen Code, GitHub Copilot CLI, Factory Droid, Crush,
  Goose, Mistral Vibe, Grok Build, Qoder CLI, Kimi Code CLI, GitLab Duo CLI,
  Rovo Dev CLI, Amp, Devin CLI / Local, Tabnine, Continue / cn,
  Visual Studio, TRAE, Roo Code, Amazon Q Developer IDE,
  CodeBuddy Code CLI, IBM Bob IDE, IBM Bob Shell, Pochi, Pi,
  Sourcegraph Cody, Oh My Pi (omp)
  Conditional/explicit targets are changed only when their documented
  platform, marker, or explicit existing config path is present.
  Manual/UI MCP boundaries: Qodo, Warp, JetBrains AI/ACP, Replit,
  Plandex, SWE-agent, BLACKBOX, GitHub cloud agents, Jules,
  CodeRabbit.

Tools: index_repository, search_graph, query_graph, trace_path,
  get_code_snippet, get_file_outline, get_graph_schema, compare_graphs,
  get_architecture, search_code, list_projects, delete_project,
  index_status, check_index_coverage, detect_changes, manage_adr,
  ingest_traces
